Link a new store entry before the store makes room (MuPDF commit 299d846, backported to 1.28.5)

This file modifies MuPDF. It is Artifex's fix for MuPDF bug 709849,
commit 299d8464f1a86df6d056e11d8850135fcac7eec7 on MuPDF master ("Bug
709849: Fix fz_store use after free.", Robin Watts, committed on
2026-10-20), with its changed lines applied unchanged to
source/fitz/store.c of the 1.28.5 source release. The Mervin PDF project
added it on 2026-10-20 in place of its own patch of 2026-10-18.
scripts/build-mupdf-linux.sh and scripts/build-mupdf-windows.ps1 apply
it after patch 0001 before building. Delete it when Mervin updates to a
MuPDF release that contains 299d846.

fz_store_item put a new fz_item into the hash table first, with
item->next == item, so the item was not in the LRU list yet. When the
store was full, it then made room. do_reap and ensure_space release
FZ_LOCK_ALLOC while they free evicted values, and only afterwards did
fz_store_item count the item's size and link it into the list with
touch(). While the lock was released, another thread could find the
item through the hash (fz_find_item, or the duplicate branch of another
fz_store_item call), and its touch() linked the item into the list.
fz_filter_store, fz_empty_store or fz_remove_item could then free it
whatever its reference count. The storing thread then ran touch() on
freed memory, or rewrote the removal chain of a filter that had not
freed the item yet.

In Mervin, two render workers can store and find the same pattern tile
(its key names the pattern, the document, the transform and the colour
space) while a closing tab filters the document's tiles out of the
store.

The commit counts the item's size and links it into the list before the
store can release the lock, and fz_store_item does not touch the item
after that. Another thread may now find the new entry, and even free it,
while the store makes room. fz_hash_insert releases the lock only to
resize the table, before it inserts the item.
newEntryFreedWhileStoreEvicts in tests/tst_mupdf_store.cpp checks it.

diff --git a/source/fitz/store.c b/source/fitz/store.c
index 171548a..7509123 100644
--- a/source/fitz/store.c
+++ b/source/fitz/store.c
@@ -528,11 +528,18 @@ fz_store_item(fz_context *ctx, void *key, void *val_, size_t itemsize, const fz_
 		val->refs++;
 	}
 
+	/* It's in the store now, as the moment we unlock below it could be found from the
+	 * hash table. */
+	store->size += itemsize;
+
+	/* Regardless of whether it's indexed, it goes into the linked list */
+	touch(store, item);
+
 	/* If we haven't got an infinite store, check for space within it */
 	if (store->max != FZ_STORE_UNLIMITED)
 	{
 		/* FIXME: Overflow? */
-		size = store->size + itemsize;
+		size = store->size;
 		if (size > store->max)
 		{
 			FZ_LOG_STORE(ctx, "Store size exceeded: item=%zu, size=%zu, max=%zu\n",
@@ -547,7 +554,7 @@ fz_store_item(fz_context *ctx, void *key, void *val_, size_t itemsize, const fz_
 					do_reap(ctx); /* Drops alloc lock */
 					fz_lock(ctx, FZ_LOCK_ALLOC);
 				}
-				size = store->size + itemsize;
+				size = store->size;
 				if (size <= store->max)
 					break;
 
@@ -572,10 +579,6 @@ fz_store_item(fz_context *ctx, void *key, void *val_, size_t itemsize, const fz_
 			FZ_LOG_DUMP_STORE(ctx, "After eviction:\n");
 		}
 	}
-	store->size += itemsize;
-
-	/* Regardless of whether it's indexed, it goes into the linked list */
-	touch(store, item);
 	fz_unlock(ctx, FZ_LOCK_ALLOC);
 
 	return NULL;
